f":"jinshu:053:s0144"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0145"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0146"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0147"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0148"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0149"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0150"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0151"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0152"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0153"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0154"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0155"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0156"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0157"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0158"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0159"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0160"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0161"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0162"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0163"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0164"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0165"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0166"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0167"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0168"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0169"},{"unitRef":"jinshu:053:s0170"}]},"unitRefs":["jinshu:053:s0142","jinshu:053:s0143","jinshu:053:s0144","jinshu:053:s0145","jinshu:053:s0146","jinshu:053:s0147","jinshu:053:s0148","jinshu:053:s0149","jinshu:053:s0150","jinshu:053:s0151","jinshu:053:s0152","jinshu:053:s0153","jinshu:053:s0154","jinshu:053:s0155","jinshu:053:s0156","jinshu:053:s0157","jinshu:053:s0158","jinshu:053:s0159","jinshu:053:s0160","jinshu:053:s0161","jinshu:053:s0162","jinshu:053:s0163","jinshu:053:s0164","jinshu:053:s0165","jinshu:053:s0166","jinshu:053:s0167","jinshu:053:s0168","jinshu:053:s0169","jinshu:053:s0170"]}},{"kind":"complete-governing-block-structure","key":"zizhitongjian:083:block:0","value":{"chapterPinRef":"zizhitongjian:083","blockIndex":0,"structure":{"type":"paragraph","sentences":[{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0001"}]},"unitRefs":["zizhitongjian:083:s0001"]}},{"kind":"complete-governing-block-structure","key":"zizhitongjian:083:block:28","value":{"chapterPinRef":"zizhitongjian:083","blockIndex":28,"structure":{"type":"paragraph","sentences":[{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0197"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0198"}]},"unitRefs":["zizhitongjian:083:s0197","zizhitongjian:083:s0198"]}},{"kind":"complete-governing-block-structure","key":"zizhitongjian:083:block:30","value":{"chapterPinRef":"zizhitongjian:083","blockIndex":30,"structure":{"type":"paragraph","sentences":[{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0200"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0201"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0202"},{"unitRef":"zizhitongjian:083:s0204"}]},"unitRefs":["zizhitongjian:083:s0200","zizhitongjian:083:s0201","zizhitongjian:083:s0202","zizhitongjian:083:s0204"]}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0001","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0001","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":0,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"愍懷太子","en":"Crown Prince Minhuai","literal":"Crown Prince Minhuai"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0142","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0142","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"喪之發也，大風雷電，幃蓋飛裂。","en":"Storm shattered funeral umbrellas.","literal":"When the hearse set out great wind and thunder came—canopies and coverings flew torn."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0143","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0143","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":1,"zh":"又為哀策曰：「皇帝臨軒，使洗馬劉務告于皇太子之殯曰：咨爾遹！","en":"They further composed a condolence text: \"The emperor facing the gallery sends Groom of the Household Liu Wu to the crown prince's lying-in-state: Ah, Yu!","literal":"They further composed a condolence text: 'The emperor facing the gallery sends Groom of the Household Liu Wu to the crown prince's lying-in-state: Ah, Yu!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0144","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0144","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":2,"zh":"幼稟英挺，芬馨誕茂。","en":"From childhood you were outstanding, and your fine qualities flourished abundantly.","literal":"You drew from youth heroic sap, fragrance ripe at birth."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0145","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0145","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":3,"zh":"既表髫齔，高明逸秀。","en":"Even in early boyhood you displayed lofty brilliance and exceptional talents.","literal":"Already in tied hair you stood lofty and bright."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0146","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0146","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":4,"zh":"昔爾聖祖，嘉爾淑美。","en":"Your august grandfather cherished your fine virtues.","literal":"Your holy ancestor prized your fine virtue."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0147","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0147","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":5,"zh":"顯詔仍崇，名振同軌。","en":"Illustrious edicts repeatedly increased your honors; your fame resounded throughout the realm.","literal":"Illustrious edicts repeatedly increased your honors; your fame resounded throughout the realm."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0148","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0148","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":6,"zh":"是用建爾儲副，永統皇基。","en":"Therefore I established you as heir, to perpetuate the imperial foundations forever.","literal":"Therefore I established you as heir, to perpetuate the imperial foundations forever."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0149","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0149","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":7,"zh":"如何凶戾潛構，禍害如茲！","en":"How did vicious cruelty secretly weave harm like this!","literal":"How did vicious cruelty secretly weave harm like this!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0150","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0150","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":8,"zh":"哀感和氣，痛貫四時。","en":"Sorrow moves harmonious qi; pain pierces four seasons.","literal":"Sorrow moves harmonious qi; pain pierces four seasons."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0151","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0151","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":9,"zh":"嗚呼哀哉！","en":"Alas, how grievous!","literal":"Alas, alas the sorrow!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0152","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0152","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":10,"zh":"爾之降廢，實我不明。","en":"Your degradation was truly due to my lack of discernment.","literal":"Your degradation was truly my blindness."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0153","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0153","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":11,"zh":"牝亂沈烖，釁結禍成。","en":"A woman’s disorder brought deep calamity; hostility accumulated and disaster took shape.","literal":"Female chaos sank calamity; omens knotted into disaster."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0154","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0154","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":12,"zh":"爾之逝矣，誰百其形？","en":"Now that you have departed, who could offer a hundredfold ransom for your person?","literal":"Now that you have departed, who could offer a hundredfold ransom for your person?"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0155","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0155","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":13,"zh":"昔之申生，含枉莫訟。","en":"Long ago Shen Sheng bore false charges, with none to plead his case.","literal":"Long ago Shen Sheng bore wrong yet could not plead."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0156","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0156","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":14,"zh":"今爾之負，抱冤於東。","en":"Now you too bear unjust blame and nurse your grievance in the east.","literal":"Now your burden of grievance hugs the eastern lands."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0157","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0157","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":15,"zh":"悠悠有識，孰不哀慟！","en":"Among all who understand, who would not grieve?","literal":"Far and near anyone with insight—who fails bitter grief!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0158","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0158","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":16,"zh":"壺關幹主，千秋悟己。","en":"The elder of Huguan remonstrated with his ruler; Qianqiu brought him to recognize his error.","literal":"The elder of Huguan remonstrated with his ruler; Qianqiu brought him to recognize his error."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0159","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0159","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":17,"zh":"異世同規，古今一理。","en":"Across different ages, the pattern is the same; past and present share one principle.","literal":"Different age, same rule—past and present one principle."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0160","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0160","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":18,"zh":"皇孫啟建，隆祚爾子。","en":"Your son has been established as imperial grandson-heir, continuing the dynastic blessing through him.","literal":"Your son has been established as imperial grandson-heir, continuing the dynastic blessing through him."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0161","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0161","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":19,"zh":"雖悴前終，庶榮後始。","en":"Though your own end was sorrowful, may the new beginning afterward be glorious.","literal":"Though front end withered, rear blossom may yet flourish."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0162","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0162","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":20,"zh":"窀穸既營，將寧爾神。","en":"Your burial chamber is now prepared, to bring your spirit peace.","literal":"Burial vault now built—we pacify your spirit."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0163","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0163","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":21,"zh":"華髦電逝，戎車雷震。","en":"Splendid plumes flash past like lightning; war chariots rumble like thunder.","literal":"Flower feathers flash like lightning; war wagons thunder."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0164","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0164","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":22,"zh":"芒芒羽蓋，翼翼縉紳。","en":"Feathered canopies stretch far and wide; the gentry advance in orderly ranks.","literal":"Vast feather-canopies; crowded sash-and-hat ranks."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0165","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0165","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":23,"zh":"同悲等痛，孰不酸辛！","en":"Courtiers weep together.","literal":"Shared grief and equal pain—who lacks bitter sorrow!"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0166","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0166","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":24,"zh":"庶光來葉，永世不泯。」","en":"May light reach posterity, never extinguished through ages.\"","literal":"May light reach posterity, never extinguished through ages.'"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0167","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0167","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":25,"zh":"諡曰湣懷。","en":"Canonized Crown Prince Minhuai.","literal":"Posthumous title Minhuai was granted."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0168","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0168","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":26,"zh":"六月己卯，葬于顯平陵。","en":"Buried sixth month at Xianping.","literal":"On jimao day of the sixth month he was buried at Xianping Mausoleum."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0169","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0169","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":27,"zh":"帝感閻纘之言，立思子台，故臣江統、陸機並作誄頌焉。","en":"Yan Zuan's plea built Son-Lament Terrace—Jiang Tong and Lu Ji wrote elegies.","literal":"Moved by Yan Zuan's words the emperor raised a Terrace of Longing for Sons; former ministers Jiang Tong and Lu Ji both composed dirges."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"jinshu:053:s0170","value":{"id":"jinshu:053:s0170","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":9,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":28,"zh":"太子三子：虨、臧、尚，並與父同幽金墉。","en":"Three sons shared Yu's prison.","literal":"The crown prince had three sons—Bin, Zang, and Shang—all imprisoned with their father at Jinyong."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0001","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0001","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":0,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"資治通鑑第083卷","en":"Zizhi Tongjian, Volume 83","literal":"Comprehensive Mirror to Aid in Government, Volume 83"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0197","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0197","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":28,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"孝惠皇帝上之下永康元年（","en":"Under Emperor Hui of Jin, Yongkang, year 1 (","literal":"The lower portion of the first reign of Emperor Xiaohui, first year of Yongkang ("}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0198","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0198","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":28,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":1,"zh":"庚申，公元三零零年）","en":"gengshen, CE 300)","literal":"gengshen, common era year 300)"}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0200","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0200","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":30,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":0,"zh":"西戎校尉司馬閻纘輿棺詣闕上書，以為：「漢戾太子稱兵拒命，言者猶曰罪當笞耳。","en":"Yan Xun, Major under the Colonel of the Western Rong, came to the palace gate with his coffin on a cart and submitted a memorial, arguing: \"When Emperor Wu's heir apparent Liu Ju took up arms in rebellion, critics still said his offense deserved only a beating.","literal":"Yan Xun, Major of the Colonel of the Western Rong, came to the gate with his coffin on a cart and submitted a memorial, holding: \"When the Han Heir Apparent Li raised troops and defied orders, those who spoke still said his crime merited only the bastinado."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0201","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0201","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":30,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":1,"zh":"今遹受罪之日，不敢失道，猶為輕於戾太子。","en":"Now Yu stands condemned yet has not strayed from duty; even so his case is still treated more leniently than that of Crown Prince Li.","literal":"Now on the day Yu received punishment he did not dare stray from the Way, yet this is still lighter than the Heir Apparent Li."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0202","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0202","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":30,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":2,"zh":"宜重選師傅，先加嚴誨，若不悛改，棄之未晚也。」書奏，不省。","en":"The court should appoint new tutors and admonish him strictly. If he does not reform, deposing him would not yet be too late.\" The memorial was submitted, but it was not examined.","literal":"One ought to choose tutors anew and first apply stern instruction; if he does not repent and reform, to discard him would not be too late.\" The memorial was submitted, but it was not examined."}},{"kind":"source-unit","key":"zizhitongjian:083:s0204","value":{"id":"zizhitongjian:083:s0204","kind":"paragraph-sentence","blockIndex":30,"collection":"sentences","itemIndex":3,"zh":"纘，圃之孫也。","en":"Xun was the grandson of Yan Pu.","literal":"Xun was the grandson of Yan Pu."}},{"kind":"person-record","key":"jinshu:053:p066","value":{"localId":"jinshu:053:p066","preferredNameSuggestion":{"en":"Yan Zuan","zh":"閻纘","pinyin":"Yan Zuan"},"historicity":"historical","descriptorSuggestion":"Official whose words moved emperor","identityHints":{"nativePlaces":[],"relatedLocalPeople":["jinshu:053:p002"],"activeDateHints":["AD 300"],"polityHints":["Western Jin","晉"]},"book":"jinshu","chapter":"053","promptVersion":7,"s